# Milestone source quality

Prefer **fewer, high-trust sources** over coverage. A milestone that is not
well corroborated is worse than no milestone.

## Bar

- Soft-reject / blacklist a host when most of its contribution is unverified,
  modeled, chart-line, or not recoupable against OFFICIAL / primary publisher /
  Wikipedia / Alinea.
- Do not keep a host just because reject-rate &lt; 50% if the remaining rows are
  mostly unverified echos or bare numbers.

## Blacklisted (do not revive)

- `vgchartz.com` (and subdomains, e.g. `gamrconnect.vgchartz.com`) — inactive in
  `trusted_source`; milestones soft-rejected. Never re-activate without an
  explicit user request.
- `nintendolife.com` — was wrongly auto-tiered OFFICIAL; mostly Japanese physical
  chart lines + media echos of figures already held elsewhere. Inactive;
  milestones soft-rejected. Never re-activate without an explicit user request.
- Modeled / review-derived estimate hosts (same treatment): `indielist.games`,
  `gamesberry.app`, `sensortower.com` (incl. `app.sensortower.com`),
  `steamdata.ai`, `playrev.io`, `gamedata.wtf`, `devuego.lat`, `devuego.es`,
  `9000.to`, `gamesensor.info` — plus AI republish farms `edgechat.ai`,
  `findings.oreate.ai`, `podcasttranscript.ai`. Also listed in
  `TAVILY_EXCLUDED_DOMAINS` so discovery does not resurface them.

## Keepers (high value)

- Publisher / official IR hosts, Wikipedia, Alinea / Rhys Elliot (see
  `alinea-milestones` rule).
